course: dictionary
lesson: 11446
title: Adhesive: things that stick
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An adhesive is anything that makes things stick together, such as glue, tape or a sticky pad. As an adjective, adhesive means sticky, able to stick to things. «Put the adhesive tape on the torn page.» Here adhesive tape is tape that sticks.
explain: The word gives you a clue: adhesive is about sticking. In «The label has a strong adhesive back», the back of the label is the part that sticks. To check your meaning, swap in sticky and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Adhesives are used in many places. «She put an adhesive bandage on her knee.» The bandage sticks to the skin to cover a cut. «Self-adhesive labels» already have a sticky back, so you peel them off and press them on.
explain: Some adhesives give off fumes, so use them in fresh air and ask a grown-up to help you. Always read the instructions on the packet first.
fact: Adhesive means sticky, able to stick to things.
fact: An adhesive is a substance like glue that makes things stick together.
fact: «Adhesive tape» is tape with sticky stuff on one side.
fact: «Self-adhesive labels» have a sticky back already, so you do not need glue.
fact: Some adhesives give off fumes, so use them in fresh air.
exercise: «The box needed a strong adhesive to hold the lid on.» What is an adhesive? | *Something that makes things stick together | A tool for cutting card | A kind of paper for drawing | A small box for keeping pens in
exercise: Which sentence still makes sense if you swap adhesive for sticky? | Mum made an adhesive cake for tea | The adhesive dog barked at the postman | The adhesive children ran down the hill | *The adhesive tape held the torn page together
exercise: Which of these is NOT an adhesive? | PVA glue | *Scissors | Adhesive tape | Glue stick
test: «Ben used a self-adhesive label on his jar.» What does self-adhesive mean? | *Sticks without wet glue, because it has a sticky back | Very heavy to lift | Made of wood | Able to clean itself
test: Why should you use some adhesives in fresh air? | Because glue needs wind to work | To make the glue dry faster in the sun | To stop the glue from smelling nice | *Some give off fumes that can make you feel unwell
exam: Which best describes an adhesive bandage? | *A plaster with a sticky back that holds a dressing on a cut | A bandage that makes a loud noise | A bandage made of wood | A bandage for tying up your hair
